# Deploy key has been used within the last 90 days
# Platform: GitHub (SDLC::DeployKey assets)
# CTN: github_deploy_key
# Frameworks: KSI-IAM, NIST IA-5(1), IA-5(13), CMMC IA.L2-3.5.7, IA.L2-3.5.10

META
    esp_id `github-deploykey-not-stale-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `github`
    criticality `medium`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `SDLC::DeployKey`

    title `Deploy key is not stale (used within 90 days)`
    description `Validates that the repository deploy key has been used within the last 90 days. Long-unused deploy keys are credentials in the wild with no observable rotation; if leaked, nobody is watching for their use, and credential-rotation policies generally do not catch them.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `github,sdlc,deploy-key,credential-hygiene,staleness,ksi-iam,nist-ia-5,cmmc-ia-l2-3.5.10`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-ELP,NIST-800-53:IA-5(1),NIST-800-53:IA-5(13),CMMC:IA.L2-3.5.7,CMMC:IA.L2-3.5.10`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-ELP,IA.L2-3.5.10`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `GitHub:scanset:identity-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Repo Settings, Deploy keys: delete keys with no recent use (days_since_last_use > 90). If the key is needed but the workflow consuming it is dormant, rotate the key and re-add the workflow; keep CI credentials short-lived rather than long-lived.`

    component_id `comp-github-sdlc`

    impl_KSI_IAM_ELP `Credential lifecycle hygiene at the SDLC platform requires that unused credentials are removed rather than retained indefinitely. The deploy keys days_since_last_use field, computed at scan time from the API-reported last_used timestamp, identifies keys that have not been used within the 90-day staleness window. The policy emits a finding for stale keys; operator action is to delete or rotate.`
    impl_IA_L2_3_5_10 `Identification and authentication credentials are protected throughout their lifecycle, including identification and removal of stale entries. Days-since-last-use is the staleness signal; the 90-day threshold gives operations a reasonable bound while allowing for legitimate dormant-CI cases to be detected and decided on.`

META_END

DEF
    # Default placeholder values, overridden per-asset by PolicySetSync
    # at bind time. PolicySetSync rewrites the SET body with one OBJECT
    # per bound deploy key (one key == one SDLC::DeployKey asset).
    VAR owner string `_unbound_`
    VAR repo string `_unbound_`
    VAR key_id int 0

    # Bound assets - managed programmatically by PolicySetSync from
    # inventory.asset_policies (status = active). Do not hand-edit;
    # the SET body is the only mutable region of this file.
    SET github_deploy_keys union
        OBJECT deploy_key_target
            owner VAR owner
            repo VAR repo
            key_id VAR key_id
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE key_not_stale
        found boolean = true
        ever_used boolean = true
        days_since_last_use int <= 90
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN github_deploy_key
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF key_not_stale
            SET_REF github_deploy_keys
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
